flang-rt: use the getpid of process.h when MinGW headers declare it

The libstdc++ headers of MinGW GCC include pthread.h of winpthreads, which
includes process.h. process.h declares int getpid(void) and defines
_CRT_GETPID_DEFINED, and the pid_t getpid() that command.cpp defines for Windows
then differs only in its return type, which fails to compile. Without the
macro, as with libc++, the source compiles unchanged. Both return the ID of the
current process.

#line restores the line numbers of the unpatched source after the change, so
the line numbers in runtime error messages, and with them the objects of every
other target, stay the same.

--- a/flang-rt/lib/runtime/command.cpp
+++ b/flang-rt/lib/runtime/command.cpp
@@ -25,7 +25,11 @@
 
 // On Windows GetCurrentProcessId returns a DWORD aka uint32_t
 #include <processthreadsapi.h>
+// process.h declares int getpid(void) and defines _CRT_GETPID_DEFINED when the
+// libstdc++ headers of MinGW GCC include it through pthread.h of winpthreads.
+#ifndef _CRT_GETPID_DEFINED
 inline pid_t getpid() { return GetCurrentProcessId(); }
+#endif
 #else
 #include <unistd.h> //getpid() unlink()
 
@@ -33,6 +37,8 @@
 #define PATH_MAX 4096
 #endif
 #endif
+// The line numbers of the unpatched source, which runtime error messages name.
+#line 36
 
 namespace Fortran::runtime {
 std::int32_t RTNAME(ArgumentCount)() {
